# LifeLink app — backend configuration
# Copy to `.env` (production build) or `.env.local` (your machine only, git-ignored).
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* values into the app at build time. Restart `npx expo start -c` after changing them.
#
# Choose ONE of the three modes:
#
# 1) DEMO mode (bundled mock data, no server) — leave EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL empty or set it to "demo".
#
# 2) LOCAL dev server (no Docker, no cloud account):
#      cd "../LifeLink Platform" && npm run dev
#    then set:
#      EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=local
#    The app finds the dev server on the computer running Metro (works in Expo Go on the same Wi-Fi).
#
# 3) PRODUCTION (your Supabase project — Dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys):
#      EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
#      EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-or-anon-key
#    NEVER put the service_role / secret key here — everything in the app is public.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
